==English==

===Etymology===
{{PIE root|en|dʰeh₁}}
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|proficiens}}, present participle of {{m|la|proficere||to go forward, advance, make progress, succeed, be profitable or useful}}, from {{m|la|pro||forth, forward}} + {{m|la|facere||to make, do}}; see {{m|en|fact}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/pɹəˈfɪʃ.ənt/}}
* {{a|GenAm}} {{IPA|en|/pɹoʊˈfɪʃ.ənt/|/pɹəˈfɪʃ.ənt/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-proficient.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Good at something; [[skilled]]; [[fluent]]; [[practiced]], especially in relation to a task or skill.
#: ''He was a '''proficient''' writer with an interest in human nature.''
#* '''1912''': {{w|Edgar Rice Burroughs}}, {{w|Tarzan of the Apes}}, Chapter 5
#*: By constant playing and experimenting with these he learned to tie rude knots, and make sliding nooses; and with these he and the younger apes amused themselves. What Tarzan did they tried to do also, but he alone originated and became '''proficient'''.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|good at}} {{l|en|skilled}}, {{l|en|fluent}}, {{l|en|practiced}}

